{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "title",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# neural-network-numpy — system architecture\n\nA feed-forward neural network in **NumPy only**, trained on two UCI tasks (banknote classification, heating-load regression) over 9 architectures × 4 optimizers × 2 learning rates × 2 batch sizes × 5 seeds = **1,440 runs**, then compared with scikit-learn, TensorFlow (Keras) and PyTorch on the same splits.\n\n**Flow:** left → right. Colored groups are stages; arrows show what feeds what. Every output file is stamped `name_YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.ext`.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": -1190,
			"width": 1800,
			"height": 400
		},
		{
			"id": "legend",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### Legend\n- **Inputs** (blue): configs and raw data\n- **Load & preprocess** (green)\n- **Training** (orange): the NumPy network\n- **nn/ library** (purple): the network itself\n- **Results** (yellow): result files\n- **Analysis & reports** (red)\n- **Library comparison** (cyan): optional dependencies\n- **Infrastructure** (grey)",
			"x": 3420,
			"y": -1190,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 400
		},
		{
			"id": "g_inputs",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Inputs",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 864,
			"height": 1394,
			"color": "#4a7bd0"
		},
		{
			"id": "configs",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### configs/\n- `classification_experiments.json`\n- `regression_experiments.json`\n\nArchitectures (layer lists, or `{\"layers\", \"max_grad_norm\"}`), optimizers, learning rates, batch sizes, seeds 42–46, epochs, early stopping (patience 10, `min_delta` 1e-4, 20-epoch guard), preprocessing.\n\n- `benchmark_experiments.json` — library model grids",
			"x": 36,
			"y": 68,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 400
		},
		{
			"id": "raw",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### data/raw/\n- `banknote_auth.csv` — 1,348 unique rows, 4 features\n- `energy_efficiency.csv` — 768 rows, 8 features → Heating_Load\n\nCommitted to the repo. **`dataset.py`** (`Fetch`) downloads them with `ucimlrepo` only if missing.",
			"x": 36,
			"y": 816,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 300
		},
		{
			"id": "g_prep",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Load & preprocess",
			"x": 1080,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 864,
			"height": 1700,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "loader",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### config_loader.py\n`ConfigLoader.load_and_validate()`\n- checks every key, layer, activation, init, dropout, seeds…\n- `normalize_architectures()` splits options (e.g. `max_grad_norm`) into `architecture_options`, so architectures stay plain layer lists",
			"x": 1116,
			"y": 68,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 300
		},
		{
			"id": "features",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### features.py + scalers.py\n`PreprocessBanknote` / `PreprocessEnergy`\n1. load & drop duplicates\n2. NumPy-only 60 / 20 / 20 train / val / test split, **stratified** for classification, per seed\n3. `StandardScaler` fit on **train only** (no leakage)\n\n→ `X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val, X_test, y_test`",
			"x": 1116,
			"y": 646,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 360
		},
		{
			"id": "plots",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### plots.py\n`Visualizer`: class balance, pairplot, correlation heatmap, target distribution, scaling before / after (first seed only)\n\n→ `reports/figures/eda/*_<stamp>.png`",
			"x": 1116,
			"y": 1326,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 200
		},
		{
			"id": "g_train",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Training (NumPy network)",
			"x": 2160,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1800,
			"height": 1802,
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "train",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### modeling/train.py — sweep orchestrator\n`main()` → for each problem × seed × architecture × optimizer × LR × batch:\n`run_single_experiment()`\n- builds the network (seeded)\n- passes the architecture's gradient cap\n- fits, evaluates on test, scores train (eval mode)\n- computes the constant-prediction **baseline**\n- records metrics, accuracy / R², timing, histories, `stop_reason`, `overfitting_epochs`, `grad_norm_history`",
			"x": 2196,
			"y": 68,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 400
		},
		{
			"id": "trainer",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### modeling/trainer.py — `Trainer`\nPer epoch: train mode → shuffle → mini-batches (forward → loss → backward → **clip** → optimizer) → eval mode → validation loss.\n- **early stopping** on validation loss (patience, `min_delta`, min-epoch guard)\n- restores the **best checkpoint** (incl. batch-norm stats)\n- stops on **divergence** (non-finite loss)\n- records `stop_reason`, overfitting signature, gradient norms",
			"x": 3096,
			"y": 68,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 400
		},
		{
			"id": "g_nn",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "nn/ — the network library (NumPy only)",
			"x": 2196,
			"y": 816,
			"width": 1728,
			"height": 952,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "network",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### network.py — `NeuralNetwork`\n`build_from_config()`, `forward()`, `backward()`, `train()` / `eval()`, `get_trainable_layers()`, `gradient_norm()`, `clip_gradients()`",
			"x": 3096,
			"y": 884,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 210
		},
		{
			"id": "layers",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### layers.py\n- `Dense` — X·W (+ b), init normal / He / Xavier\n- `BatchNorm` — γ, β, running stats, train / eval\n- `Dropout` — inverted, own seeded RNG",
			"x": 2808,
			"y": 1394,
			"width": 300,
			"height": 200
		},
		{
			"id": "actloss",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### activations.py · losses.py\nReLU, Sigmoid, Tanh, Linear · BCE, MSE — each with a hand-derived backward pass",
			"x": 3384,
			"y": 1394,
			"width": 280,
			"height": 200
		},
		{
			"id": "optim",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### optimizers.py\nSGD · momentum (moving average) · **AdaBelief** · **Muon** (orthogonalized momentum) — update every parameter of every layer",
			"x": 2232,
			"y": 884,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 210
		},
		{
			"id": "metrics",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### metrics.py\nBCE, MSE, accuracy, R² — used by the trainer, train.py and **every** library model",
			"x": 2232,
			"y": 1394,
			"width": 300,
			"height": 200
		},
		{
			"id": "g_results",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Results",
			"x": 4176,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 864,
			"height": 1020,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "results",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### reports/main_results_full_<stamp>.json\nOne record per run (1,440): settings, test / train / baseline metrics, best epoch, stop reason, loss + gradient-norm histories, fit time",
			"x": 4212,
			"y": 510,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 260
		},
		{
			"id": "summary",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### reports/main_summary_<stamp>.csv\nCompact table: problem, seed, optimizer, batch, LR, architecture, epochs ran, best epoch, stop reason, test metric",
			"x": 4212,
			"y": 68,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 200
		},
		{
			"id": "g_analysis",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Analysis & reports",
			"x": 5256,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 864,
			"height": 1394,
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "comparisons",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### comparisons.py\nMatched loss-curve plots (seed 42): optimizers, depth, learning rate, A2 variants, dropout — with convergence + best-epoch markers\n\n→ `reports/figures/comparisons/*.png`\n→ `reports/comparisons/*.txt`",
			"x": 5292,
			"y": 68,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 320
		},
		{
			"id": "analysis",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### analysis.py\nConvergence epoch vs. best epoch, normalized losses, A2 variants & collapse checks, dropout + generalization gap, **multi-seed** mean ± std, model selection on validation, stopping & overfitting table\n\n→ `reports/analysis_<stamp>.txt`",
			"x": 5292,
			"y": 680,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 400
		},
		{
			"id": "g_bench",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Library comparison — nn_numpy/benchmarks (optional: scikit-learn, TensorFlow, PyTorch)",
			"x": 1080,
			"y": 2040,
			"width": 5040,
			"height": 952,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "bdata",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### benchmarks/data.py\n`load_splits(problem, seed)` reuses the main pipeline's preprocessing → **identical** splits and baselines for every library",
			"x": 1116,
			"y": 2142,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 240
		},
		{
			"id": "sk",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### sklearn_models.py\nlogistic / ridge, SVM / SVR, random forest, gradient boosting, MLP — small grids",
			"x": 3240,
			"y": 2142,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 140
		},
		{
			"id": "keras",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### keras_models.py\nA1, A2, A2-bias, A2-bn rebuilt in Keras (framework defaults, EarlyStopping)",
			"x": 3240,
			"y": 2431,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 140
		},
		{
			"id": "torch",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### torch_models.py\nSame architectures in PyTorch, hand-written loop with the NumPy trainer's early-stopping rule",
			"x": 3240,
			"y": 2720,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 140
		},
		{
			"id": "brun",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### benchmarks/run.py\n`python -m nn_numpy.benchmarks.run [sklearn|tensorflow|pytorch]` — every model × grid × seed, selected on validation, scored with `nn/metrics.py`. `benchmarks/tuning.py` (`make tune`) also tunes the Keras and PyTorch models with Optuna",
			"x": 2196,
			"y": 2142,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 260
		},
		{
			"id": "bresults",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### reports/benchmark_<library>_results_<stamp>.json\nOne file per library",
			"x": 4212,
			"y": 2142,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 200
		},
		{
			"id": "breport",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### benchmarks/report.py\nTables (mean ± std), per-seed head-to-heads, same-architecture NumPy vs. Keras vs. PyTorch tables\n\n→ `reports/benchmark_report_<stamp>.txt`\n→ `reports/figures/benchmarks/*.png` (bar charts, learning curves)",
			"x": 5292,
			"y": 2142,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 380
		},
		{
